<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55862" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατευθύ</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>straight forward</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κ. ὁρᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					5.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Jud.Voc.</u>
				11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν κ. ἔρχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					2.11.3
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ.τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.3b
				</span></i>
			; <i>on the same side</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰθύς</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὁ κ. δίδυμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ruf.
				</span></i>
			(?) ap.<i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				3.45
			</span></i>. (Better written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽
			εὐθύ</span>.)</div>
